  "text": "Sol read his unfinished draft. The others listened to the page he had brought, and its ending stayed open for him to work on.\n\nHe raised the bird and looked underneath. Then he turned it toward me. “You can see where we fixed it.” “Yes,” I said.\n\nWork beside Grandma: draw through the soil, place the seed, then cover it. Keyboard controls handle the same objects.\n\nWe checked the flour after you left. It was dry. Then we made dough from it. Your page stops before that part.\n\nSol has brought a draft of his story. After he reads it, we can tell him what we'd like to hear more about.\n\nI can still hear the rain outside. It sounds different when you aren’t trying to catch it.\n\nSol wants to come. He'd like to read his draft and ask what people want to know next.\n\n“Grandma says you hardly visit. She thinks you don’t enjoy going there anymore.”\n\nWe’re starting after the last boat returns. I’ll read while you listen.\n\nYou could read your draft and ask what people want to hear more about.\n\nWe’re starting after the last boat returns. Would you read your story?\n\nSol and I worked on the ending of his story. He's ready to share it.\n\nSol wants to come. We finished his story, and he'd like to read it.\n\nWould you tell everyone how the repair helped Rina bake the bread?\n\nSol has brought A Small Repair and the ending we chose together.\n\nWe’re keeping the usual time. I’ll read your story for you.\n\nWould you tell everyone about Rina’s thank-you visit?\n\nI'll ask Grandma to start the next gathering later.\n\nI can bring you a story if you’re still working.\n\nWas Rina able to bake the bread she promised?\n\nContinue the conversation at Sol’s workshop.\n\nWhat would you like to do with your message?\n\nCould we start after the last boat returns?\n\nLet’s talk about why Mara stopped visiting.",
